# What EAS Build uploads for the mobile app.
#
# EAS archives the whole git repository, not just JSAN-AUTO-TRACKING. This repo also carries the
# backend, the admin panel and ~250 MB of customer GIS data (p1vc-roads alone is 168 MB), which
# made every build a ~194 MB upload that failed partway on an ordinary connection. The app is
# about 2 MB.
#
# Everything that is not the app is listed BY NAME. The tidier "ignore /*, then re-include
# !/JSAN-AUTO-TRACKING/" is not supported by EAS's matcher: it silently produced an EMPTY
# archive and a build that failed before installing anything. Check with
#   npx eas build:inspect --platform android --profile preview --stage archive --output <dir>
# after touching this file. A new top-level folder of data must be added here, or it ships.
#
# When this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, so the app's own ignore rules are
# repeated below. /android and /ios matter most: they are generated on the build server
# (continuous native generation), and uploading the local copies would make EAS build from those
# instead of regenerating them.

# ── Not the app ──
/.claude/
/admin-panel/
/backend/
/core-tracking-code/
/docs/
/scripts/
/Final Merge/
/FinalMerge0708/
/P2/
/QLD_P2_RMOB_Nav_new/
/p1vc-polygons/
/p1vc-roads/
/*.zip
/*.geojson
/*.csv
/*.md
/*.txt

# ── The app's own .gitignore, anchored to its folder ──
node_modules/
/JSAN-AUTO-TRACKING/.expo/
/JSAN-AUTO-TRACKING/dist/
/JSAN-AUTO-TRACKING/web-build/
/JSAN-AUTO-TRACKING/expo-env.d.ts
/JSAN-AUTO-TRACKING/.kotlin/
/JSAN-AUTO-TRACKING/app-example
/JSAN-AUTO-TRACKING/ios
/JSAN-AUTO-TRACKING/android
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
*.pem
.env*.local
*.tsbuildinfo
